      "path": "/usr/local/var/cyclotron/tmp.noindex/cyclotron-d11fe31e/samples/7bb0a9f1357b/elex-renamed-viewer.exe",
      "sha256": "7bb0a9f1357b17ac133fcf6ff03db54422ee1a2501184e351229e1a71fdabecd",
      "verdict": "MALICIOUS",
      "marker": "Elex stager: hides decoded DLL; launches a renamed rundll32",
      "identification": "Modified Elex-style native x86 resource DLL stager; unsigned, MSVC/MFC, renamed packed sections and rebuilt imports.",
      "execution": [
        "CRT entry 0x42e704 reaches MFC InitInstance at 0x401830. With no argument, 0x401220 copies its own image to a random temp executable, appends padding, starts cmd /c ping 127.0.0.1 -n 2&<temp> <original>, and exits. The argument branch calls 0x401450.",
        "0x401450 loads GUI resource 130, dispatches byte subtraction by index modulo three at 0x4014d5, and prepares a random directory under D: or C: Program Files. SetFileAttributesA receives immediate 2 at 0x4015d4, marking the directory Hidden.",
        "It writes the decoded resource to a random DLL, appends padding, repairs MZ at offset zero, copies c:\\windows\\system32\\rundll32.exe to a random executable, formats %s \"%s\",Review %s, and calls CreateProcessA at 0x401814 on WinSta0\\Default.",
        "The 91,144-byte resource statically decodes with residues (141,31,110), followed by MZ repair. It is a valid x86 DLL with an NRV2B-style unpacking loop at 0x10030760; offline decompression and E8/E9 restoration recovered 190,005 bytes. The export is Viewer at RVA 0xbb50, with obfuscated jump/stack dispatch."
      ],
      "verdict_evidence": "The concealed resource DLL and renamed trusted execution host establish deceptive payload staging independently of the family label or final payload. Ordinary software installation does not explain this combination of custom resource hiding, hidden random paths, a renamed system loader and delayed self-relaunch.",
      "limits": "The batch sample changes the parent command export from Viewer to Review (10 bytes differ from the existing positive fixture, including a second string copy), while the embedded DLL still exports Viewer. This can prevent the intended export call; success is not required for the malicious staging verdict. No claim of successful C2, credential theft or service installation is added from recovered strings alone. Origin, operator and deployment remain unknown.",
